# Local-only env. Never commit; never package.
#
# Files merge convention (matches BXM/UJM):
#   The "Default Values" section is overwritten on every `npx omega setup`.
#   The "Custom Values" section is preserved verbatim — put your secrets there.
#   Existing values for keys that appear in both sections stay in their original section.
#   Values are normalized to double-quoted form on every merge (handles spaces / special chars).

# ========== Default Values ==========
# Commented keys are PLACEHOLDERS: values resolve through the .env cascade
# (shell > this file > brand root .env > company .env) — uncomment here only
# to override for THIS target. An empty value never claims a key.

# ─── GitHub ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GH_TOKEN=

# ─── Backend Manager ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OMEGA_ADMIN_KEY=

# ─── macOS signing + notarization ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Point CSC_LINK at config/certs/developer-id-application.p12 (per-brand cert file).
# See docs/signing.md or config/certs/README.md for full setup.
# CSC_LINK=
# CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=

# Notarization (App Store Connect API key)
# APPLE_API_KEY=
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_API_ISSUER=
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=

# ─── Windows signing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signing strategy is set in config/omega.json5 (`platforms.win.signing.strategy`):
# self-hosted (default) | cloud | local.
#
# Self-hosted (EV USB token): set the cert thumbprint, the SafeNet token PIN,
# and signtool path. These get pushed to GH Actions secrets by `npx omega push-secrets`
# and injected into the windows-sign workflow job.
#
# Find your cert thumbprint on the runner host:
#   Get-ChildItem -Path Cert:\CurrentUser\My | Format-Table Subject, Thumbprint
# WIN_EV_TOKEN_PATH=
# WIN_CSC_KEY_PASSWORD=
# SIGNTOOL_PATH=

# ─── Snap Store (Linux) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required only when `platforms.linux.snap.enabled = true` in omega.json5.
# Mint locally with: `snapcraft export-login -` (writes a credentials blob to stdout).
# Paste the entire blob (multi-line) into the value below — `mgr push-secrets` flows
# it to GH Actions where the workflow uses it for `electron-builder` snap publish.
# SNAPCRAFT_STORE_CREDENTIALS=

# ─── Google Analytics 4 (GA4 Measurement Protocol) ──────────────────────────
# Measurement ID goes in config/omega.json5 (analytics.providers.google.id).
# The API secret lives here — never in committed config. Webpack bakes it into
# packaged builds at build time so production apps don't need this file.
# Mint a secret in GA4 Admin → Data Streams → your stream → Measurement Protocol API secrets.
# GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_SECRET=

# ─── @omega.js/desktop test framework ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by integration tests. Optional — tests skip if empty.
# OMEGA_TEST_FIREBASE_ADMIN_KEY=
OMEGA_TEST_USER_UID="desktop-test-user"

# ========== Custom Values ==========

# Anything below this line is yours and won't be touched by `npx omega setup`.
